<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel kills six in Gaza hospital strike as 9-month-old baby freezes to death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bafc67b848336648b7ed3a9db876d1ca9d6bd9da78f97684dd3a8eec222ddfb4</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:18:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death--43c83484c699.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death" /><summary type="html">An overnight Israeli air strike on Nasser Hospital in southern Gaza killed at least six Palestinians Thursday, including a teenage boy and a surgeon, medics said. Elsewhere in the devastated Palestinian territory, a nine-month-old baby died from the cold as families flee worsening flooding.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>How FRANCE 24 traced Tehran-backed Afghan fighters from Syria to southeastern Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7399c2d12f6f642e10df902dd0562beb9d17fb633d5423ddce8e7cd4f66099c0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:03:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-iran-afghan-fatemiyoun-fighters-syria-baluchistan" /><summary type="html">Members of the Tehran-backed Afghan Shia militia known as the Fatemiyoun division have resurfaced in Iran after largely disappearing from public view following the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s government in Syria in 2024. FRANCE 24 used "martyrdom” announcements and the geolocation of videos shared on social media to trace their presence.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli occupation in southern Lebanon: Displaced families struggle to cope</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c35ec669fc9be8817b5c4a156220bcdc319d3f504887460fcfcf78fd3d2dc1d</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:51:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261112-israeli-occupation-in-southern-lebanon-displaced-families-struggle-to-cope--b0f3878e931e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261112-israeli-occupation-in-southern-lebanon-displaced-families-struggle-to-cope" /><summary type="html">In Lebanon, more than 360,000 people are still displaced after months of war between Israel and Hezbollah, according to the UN. Along the border, the Israeli army claims to be fighting the Iran-backed militant group but now occupies 6 percent of Lebanese territory and is wiping entire villages off the map. In the border area, we meet families living in makeshift housing. Many fear they may never go home.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot unveils agenda to reverse Netanyahu’s policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7c268d86d19a6758b40ca4704c1e731045650b33b5a301971b63296c519cd00</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T22:13:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261111-gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies--0f9f16f8a604.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261111-gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies" /><summary type="html">The bloc of Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot introduced a series of bills at the start of the legislative session that target Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his policies. They include launching an official government-led inquiry into the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks, setting term limits on the position of prime minister and overturning changes the outgoing Netanyahu-led government made to limit the powers of the judiciary. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Rina Bassist, Editor at Al-Monitor.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot unveils agenda to reverse Netanyahu’s policies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6b17646f63edf03cc75f07811e439301e688574efefdf20aba4df0f8c3d56901</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T22:11:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies--8332c2c1dd5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies" /><summary type="html">The bloc of Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot introduced a series of bills at the start of the legislative session that target Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his policies. They include launching an official government-led inquiry into the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks, setting term limits on the position of prime minister and overturning changes the outgoing Netanyahu-led government made to limit the powers of the judiciary. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Rina Bassist, Editor at Al-Monitor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eisenkot quickly targets Netanyahu's legacy in new Israeli parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:608aae0a735a0c240c211eb40f8a5d3dd51a1076aa1a0e05693e7a76332ddaca</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:29:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eisenkot-quickly-targets-netanyahu-s-legacy-in-new-israeli-parliament--38561be2e3bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eisenkot-quickly-targets-netanyahu-s-legacy-in-new-israeli-parliament" /><summary type="html">Israeli ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot and his allies launched a legislative onslaught against caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's legacy on Tuesday, as a new parliament convened in a heated first session.</summary></entry><entry><title>Egyptian journalist Lina Attalah faces prison as trial sparks international outcry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78ad3fffb6b35f3e86ebf8d89a5df4cca9474a9131ddfaab1b3ecc7c731fca33</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T01:53:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261111-lina-attalah-egypt-trial-prison--3613bd1908b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261111-lina-attalah-egypt-trial-prison" /><summary type="html">Egyptian journalist Lina Attalah, head of independent news outlet Mada Masr, faces a criminal court retrial Wednesday over charges of operating without a licence and publishing false news. The UN criticised Egypt’s “widening assaults on press freedom” Tuesday. Attalah was previously handed a one-year prison sentence in absentia in 2024.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Eisenkot pushes October 7 inquiry as Netanyahu targets Arab parties in tense new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be5dde9c85c0b666f301efadc2aca76f6495c83c985749e3dff937debb17187b</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:53:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-eisenkot-pushes-october-7-inquiry-as-netanyahu-targets-arab-parties-in-tense-new-parliament--2295d5ce6f71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-eisenkot-pushes-october-7-inquiry-as-netanyahu-targets-arab-parties-in-tense-new-parliament" /><summary type="html">Gadi Eisenkot, the politician tasked with forming a new Israeli government, pledged on Tuesday to launch an official inquiry into Hamas's October 7, 2023 attacks and reverse many of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's policies as the new parliament was sworn in a tense opening session that saw rival parties trade barbs over the possibility of forming a government with the support of Arab lists.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Asymmetric cyberwarfare: 'States increasingly use cyberattacks in support of their other objectives'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55e1199fe97ffeb286006c00b1d4943c9784991fc8a300aaeed22fb1d7a10f3d</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:25:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives--937e2d10d52d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Rafe Pilling, Director of Threat Intelligence in the Sophos Counter Threat Unit (CTU). How can a minor cyber intrusion disrupt food supplies, expose the weaknesses of industrial infrastructure and become an instrument of geopolitical confrontation? The cyberattacks targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in France offer a revealing illustration of how digital vulnerabilities can translate into tangible economic disruption and potentially broader threats to society. As Pilling explains, “With a small amount of effort from the adversary side, they can create a large impact, in this case destroying food and producing empty shelves or empty refrigeration units in stores.” This asymmetry lies at the heart of contemporary cyber conflict, in which modest technical interventions can produce disproportionate economic and operational consequences</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu bloc targets Arab lawmakers as Israel's new parliament is sworn in</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3f31aa1728da7c5d539c05f8ad9867cddd033810b8294f9bbf6cb49d7b5c858</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T14:40:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-live-new-israeli-parliament-sworn-in-eisenkot-aims-to-form-government-netanyahu-knesset--fb2f0ccfa09f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-live-new-israeli-parliament-sworn-in-eisenkot-aims-to-form-government-netanyahu-knesset" /><summary type="html">Tensions ran high at the first session of Israel's new parliament on Tuesday as rival camps traded barbs over the possibility of ruling with the support of Arab lists. The party of opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot, who has been tasked with forming a government, moved to immediately set up a commission to investigate Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack, an action long resisted by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>New Israel parliament to be sworn in as Eisenkot works to form new govt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b56fda5b90f8e197979adad0dab832743f39d102f3e1fd44c3e4a849465b50dc</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:22:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-new-israel-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-works-to-form-new-govt--82de353b7556.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-new-israel-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-works-to-form-new-govt" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament will be sworn on Tuesday, November 10, with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu set to lose his majority as rival Gadi Eisenkot works to form a new government. The opposition hopes to use its newfound legislative power to move quickly on key priorities, including a commission to investigate security failures under Netanyahu that allowed the October 7, 2023 attack by Hamas. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's new parliament to be sworn in as Eisenkot prepares government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecd10d3a3f9028f2718907f6b6114bf8fc88ea9d98db6963def2158c30b4e19c</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T09:17:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-israel-s-new-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-forms-government--637eebbf9862.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-israel-s-new-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-forms-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's new parliament is set to be sworn in Tuesday with neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's bloc nor opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot's camp holding a majority. Eisenkot seeks to build a coalition after receiving a mandate to form a government.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Will Eisenkot succeed in 'minefield of Israeli politics' where 'so many other generals' have failed?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a66a82898c17b7e17990ce353dbfb6585f713ef77bb0155b3378effb9307f176</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T20:03:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-fa--ea02cbc16553.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-failed" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Dahlia Scheindlin, Israeli political analyst, strategic consultant and pollster, to examine a question that reaches far beyond the immediate struggle for power: Can Israel move beyond PM Benjamin Netanyahu amid coalition deadlock, growing disillusionment in Washington and the persistent limits of political inclusion?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>'We think' the Iranians and Americans want to negotiate, Egyptian FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f91abdd832e274910d2de88e5f19a1fededc460ba19d3c0f8c87fcb0645bf3b0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T19:31:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261109-we-think-the-iranians-and-americans-want-to-negotiate-egyptian-fm-says--3e2f1e24b9a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261109-we-think-the-iranians-and-americans-want-to-negotiate-egyptian-fm-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Egyptian Foreign Minister Badr Abdelatty said he believed Iran and the United States wanted to negotiate, but called for a "concrete deal" to prevent another escalation. He also said Cairo was still "counting" on US President Donald Trump to "move forward" with the stalled Gaza peace plan and was "confident" US military aid to Egypt would continue.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>'Life in Gaza simply miserable': Amid flooding, lack of aid, conditions 'worsen' for Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf25fac92721a28ed87c0918d624ee3a733f2aefe3f27a31a6fb81a8548013ad</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T17:26:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians--d44b8a8693f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Shaina Low, Communication Adviser for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC). Thirteen months into what she describes as a "so-called ceasefire," the humanitarian crisis in Gaza continues to deepen, exposing the profound gap between diplomatic commitments and the lived realities of Palestinian civilians. In an interview with France 24, Shayna Low, communications adviser in Palestine for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), describes a population confronting winter flooding, repeated displacement, deteriorating shelter conditions and persistent restrictions on humanitarian assistance. "Life in Gaza is simply miserable." Low urges Israel to "open all the crossings, lift the restrictions, let aid in."</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran 'has mistaken perception' of US midterm result, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c1eb7fa9cfe5cccc58f8966ead944a8556916ecc5bb879f929ea639837dd96a</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T13:49:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says--83d8e60dc207.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says" /><summary type="html">A leading commentator on Iran says the country sees the results of the US midterm elections as giving them a golden opportunity for a sweet deal. Paymon Azmoudeh from Forward Global was speaking amid conflicting statements from the key players about whether there will be further US military action in Iran. President Donald Trump says that renewed strikes on Iran are "highly unlikely" if talks progress. However, Iran's foreign minister says the midterms have brought a ⁠pause to mediators' work.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia intercepts Houthi missiles as Riyadh's Aramco building damaged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f75f4f65c8ec849a4d831b60839a3b5e55bc6ec27fe298c4ae5af2c2e4cfafc3</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:41:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-saudi-arabia-intercepts-houthi-missiles-as-riyadh-s-aramco-building-damaged--908b03ae8d4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-saudi-arabia-intercepts-houthi-missiles-as-riyadh-s-aramco-building-damaged" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia intercepted incoming missiles from Yemen's Houthi rebels targeting the kingdom's capital and other regions on Sunday, November 8, with falling debris damaging a building belonging to the state-owned oil giant Aramco in Riyadh’s financial district.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has six weeks to form a government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a386bc55d73c1038131281abe5307a69e7fc0a82bfc6bccf630c065c764ff695</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T10:36:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-israel-s-opposition-leader-gadi-eisenkot-has-six-weeks-to-form-a-government--4fa49cb09b7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-israel-s-opposition-leader-gadi-eisenkot-has-six-weeks-to-form-a-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog formally gave opposition politician Gadi Eisenkot the first chance to form the next government Sunday evening, leaving Eisenkot six weeks to try to put together a coalition to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli opposition leader Eisenkot begins the hard work of forging a coalition government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc4974c0e9182bb11a4ea0c8bf24f30b84bf344730dc5b4e46ef28677e49f66e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T21:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government--f27d5923499e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot was tapped by President Isaac Herzog to try to form a government Sunday evening. But his lack of a clear majority in parliament will make trying to forge a coalition alongside the country's divided minor parties an uphill struggle.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Gadi Eisenkot receives mandate to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e835fd7a2b70191bdcbca0d962044390f2e6a01799b7b8bfa67440ba5b5164d8</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T16:58:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government--3797dae49af9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has officially been tasked with forming the country's next government, following a formal announcement by President Isaac Herzog. He now has up to six weeks to negotiate with potential coalition partners and secure a parliamentary majority. While an alliance with Arab Israeli parties appears to be the easiest option mathematically, it remains politically sensitive. Eisenkot must now navigate difficult negotiations to build a coalition capable of replacing Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1f0433e92837a19a42945ceb4edc0e386b19b35a4d346bc75811d54bde945b2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:22:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens--95e6e91a4caa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens" /><summary type="html">One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli president officially tasks Eisenkot with forming government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6788f24e1785dca40e7e688cdf0d8b9509086950cbbcdb7e01f4a0816111d6c</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:47:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-ne--c83bf488fa4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-netanyahu-coalition-government-elections" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Sunday officially tasked ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot with trying to form a government after neither Eisenkot's bloc nor that or incumbent Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu won a clear majority in Israel's October 27 elections. Eisenkot now has up to six weeks to form a coalition government. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Arab-led parties gain influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8918e7ff6ad182ccd2f69ed346640ffd77e52f169a81f8a7e3f55a57117256ad</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:43:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence--0c9b38b79b08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence" /><summary type="html">Arab-led parties have endorsed Gadi Eisenkot despite his ruling out a coalition with them. Their support is driven by a shared goal: removing Benjamin Netanyahu from power. But could these parties ultimately hold the balance of power in forming Israel's next government? Antonia Kerrigan reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gaza: Heavy rain inundates thousands of tents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2238a31ab76de30907ba6c4eaf48ce13ddfd83676415c5de639d3b685dcf621e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:42:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents--9e19bbe6af60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents" /><summary type="html">Heavy rainfall has flooded thousands of tents sheltering displaced Palestinians across the Gaza Strip, including in Deir al-Balah. Residents say overflowing sewage has mixed with the floodwater, further worsening already dire living conditions. Families are struggling to salvage their belongings, building makeshift earthen barriers and trying to drain the water by hand. Many have seen essential items soaked and rendered unusable, adding to the hardship faced by those already displaced.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis claim attack on Aramco skyscraper in Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:040fe2268f7a1eb13ea8421038c1dc3ca34840a7d66f54120643e70c6eb81244</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T08:11:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-yemen-s-houthis-claim-attack-on-aramco-building-in-riyadh-s-financial-district--fcf5a21a0bd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-yemen-s-houthis-claim-attack-on-aramco-building-in-riyadh-s-financial-district" /><summary type="html">A skyscraper belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco was hit by a Houthi-claimed attack on Sunday, blowing out windows across several floors but causing no casualties. The Iran-aligned group has repeatedly targeted Aramco facilities and infrastructure.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli president picks Netanyahu's rival Eisenkot to try to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b26fd3390e48f159d3ce53780ce99a6c7ae1687b02aa5bc7d6847c8ba92dcf96</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:37:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government--bea9f93a0c67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog picked former military chief Gadi Eisenkot to try to form a government, he said in a statement Saturday. Last month's parliamentary elections left neither Eisenkot nor Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu with a clear path to building a majority.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel coalition talks gain momentum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e247ba34f55cadb6989a4a33460c004d84f503718428465fa38e3adcbab9a91</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T12:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum--e112145ab913.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-coalition-talks-gain-momentum" /><summary type="html">Following inconclusive elections in Israel, opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot says he is confident of securing the mandate to form a government, as President Isaac Herzog prepares to nominate the first candidate. Eisenkot claims he is making progress in efforts to oust long-serving Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: 30 dead in strikes on Taiz market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:081033a2e3721af850ba7d30f08afc7d4e5312a4f2d86b841dab49d63d833bbb</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T09:37:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market--556471887193.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-30-dead-in-strikes-on-taiz-market" /><summary type="html">At least 30 people have reportedly been killed in an attack on a market in Yemen’s Taiz province, with Houthi rebels blaming Saudi airstrikes. Government forces and local authorities have disputed the claim, instead accusing the Houthis of indiscriminate fire. The province has witnessed intense clashes in recent weeks and is home to around half of the more than 300,000 people displaced by the latest fighting. Caroline Baum reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Is Israel opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot going to replace Benjamin Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23968e87f9b4da53d2efba870498f4ee1be56468af11c23381a455e555d41120</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:25:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-is-israel-opposition-figure-gadi-eisenkot-going-to-replace-benjamin-netanyahu--06fb66f266f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-is-israel-opposition-figure-gadi-eisenkot-going-to-replace-benjamin-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">In Israel, Gadi Eisenkot emerged on Thursday, November 5, as the frontrunner to be tasked with forming a government. This comes after one of the two main parties representing ultra-Orthodox Jewish voters – a longtime ally of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's coalition – declined to recommend any candidate for the task. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's Eisenkot claims 'progress' in coalition talks as opposition eases on ultra-Orthodox draft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8dc5f0ad07d5b6512a0087fed4a0d80ef04c84a5eeef0d092b62b19922e4277</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T11:43:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261106-israel-s-eisenkot-claims-significant-progress-in-coalition-talks-as-opposition-eases-on-ult--688a89e5ca21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261106-israel-s-eisenkot-claims-significant-progress-in-coalition-talks-as-opposition-eases-on-ultra-orthodox-draft" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition candidate Gadi Eisenkot said on Friday he was making "significant progress" in forming a government to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu as one of his possible coalition partners walked back demands that ultra-Orthodox Jews complete military service and signalled a willingness to hold talks with the community.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
